\section{Introduction}\label{sec:biblio-intro}

This chapter provides a guided tour of the literature on programming language theory, compiler design, type theory, semantics, program analysis, and category theory for computer science. For each area, we identify the key texts, explain their contributions, and suggest how they relate to the material in this book. The goal is to help the reader navigate the vast literature and find the sources most relevant to their interests.

